{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "iterative",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 16, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 14, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.15,
      "why": "Lowest-power family, but throughput is Fmax/(N+3). To reach 50 MSPS it needs a very high Fmax and small N. This narrow range tests the only plausible feasible corner (N=10..14) while keeping W small enough to limit area/power. If no point meets both 50 MSPS and 2^-12 error, iterative is infeasible for this spec."
    },
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 22, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "k", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.85,
      "why": "Main sequential candidate for 50 MSPS. Throughput is Fmax/(ceil(N/k)+3), so k>1 is needed to reduce cycles. The range covers k=2..8 and N=10..22, which spans the trade-off between throughput (higher k, lower N), accuracy (higher N, W, guards), and power (smaller area/frequency). W and N are kept moderate to focus on the low-power corner while still allowing enough accuracy for 2^-12."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec demands 50 MSPS and max error <= 2^-12. Accuracy depends only on data_width, n_iter, angle_guard, frac_guard and rounding, so all families share the same accuracy trade-off. Iterative is the lowest-power family but its throughput is Fmax/(N+3); meeting 50 MSPS requires either very small N or an unrealistically high Fmax. We allocate a small budget (15%) to test the only plausible iterative corner (N=10..14, W=12..16). Unrolled_k is the main sequential family that can reach 50 MSPS by processing k micro-rotations per cycle; we allocate 85% to it, covering k=2..8 and N=10..22 to map the Pareto front between power, throughput and accuracy. The ranges are chosen to include the minimum design that can meet the constraints, so the search can find the lowest-power feasible point, while still covering enough accuracy margin to avoid missing the front."
}

{
  "decision": "add_family",
  "next_plan": {
    "families": [
      {
        "budget_share": 0.6,
        "family": "pipelined_m",
        "ranges": [
          {"choices": ["round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 12, "param": "data_width"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 22, "low": 12, "param": "n_iter"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 3, "low": -1, "param": "angle_guard"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 6, "low": 2, "param": "m"}
        ]
      ,
      "why": "1 result/cycle; only pipelined families can reach 50 MSPS. Low m keeps FF count (and power) down while still hitting the throughput floor; data_width/n_iter ranges keep accuracy >= ~12.3 bits."
      },
      {
        "budget_share": 0.4,
        "family": "pipelined",
        "ranges": [
          {"choices": ["round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 12, "param": "data_width"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 22, "low": 12, "param": "n_iter"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 3, "low": -1, "param": "angle_guard"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"}
        ],
        "why": "Always-1-result/cycle reference point for the front; N+2 latency but the same per-cycle throughput, so it bounds the accuracy/power trade-off against pipelined_m."
      }
    ]
  ,
  "rationale": "Every evaluation so far is a multi-cycle family and the throughput constraint is violated by 100% of designs, best only 11.5 MSPS (iterative) and 7.77 MSPS (unrolled_k). That is not a parameter-tuning failure: iterative costs N+3 cycles/result and unrolled_k ceil(N/k)+3, so even the best observed 11.5 MSPS is ~4x short of 50 MSPS and cannot be closed by width/guard tweaks. The registry's 1-result-per-cycle families (pipelined, pipelined_m) are exactly the untried options that can clear 50 MSPS, while the accuracy side is already proven reachable (best max_abs_err 2^-15.92, comfortably inside the 2^-12 limit). So the constraint is reachable only by switching family, not by refining the current ranges. Spend the remaining ~40 evals on pipelined_m (higher share, low m to control FFs/power) plus pipelined as the reference point, with data_width 12-20 and n_iter 12-22 to hold accuracy at or above the 12-bit requirement with a little margin, then map the front if a feasible region appears."
}  



  ,
  "rationale": ""
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Final round, budget exhausted (100/100 evals, HV = 0, 0 feasible designs). The only hard blocker is throughput: 100% of evaluations violate throughput_msps >= 50, and the best value seen anywhere is 16.1 MSPS (unrolled_k), a ~3.1x shortfall; the accuracy constraint is clearly reachable (best max_abs_err 5.51e-08 = 2^-24.11, far inside 2^-12). However, I cannot honestly declare `infeasible`: the registry's throughput lever is results/cycle, and the two families actually evaluated (iterative, unrolled_k) are both multi-cycle-per-result by construction, so their ~5-16 MSPS ceiling is expected and says nothing about the pipelined/pipelined_m families, which emit 1 result/cycle (throughput = Fmax) and were never evaluated in this run. With no Fmax/throughput numbers for those families in the summaries, claiming no registry design can reach 50 MSPS would be inventing evidence. So the empty front is an exploration/budget artifact, not a proven infeasibility, and the correct terminal action is `stop` rather than `infeasible`. If the loop were reopened, the decisive next step would be to evaluate pipelined and pipelined_m (1 result/cycle) with data_width ~14-18, n_iter ~12-16, angle_guard 0..3, frac_guard 0..2, rounding=round, since those are the only families whose throughput can plausibly clear 50 MSPS while holding max_abs_err <= 2^-12."
  ,
  "next_plan": null
}
